# the snippet database: find's enumeration with no target, one program
# per column of values on 32 fixed points, kept for the session or in
# NAME.snip, grown a level of cost at a time and read back to go on
snippets grow inputs 2 width 32 cost 3
# find's own bank (1024 points) is full before it reaches this cost-3
# program; the database's 32 points reach every program of cost 3
f(a: u32, b: u32) = ((a + b) | (a - b)) & ~((a + b) & (a - b))
find f 1
find f 1 snippets
# a function with no program of cost 3 or less in the database
g(a: u32, b: u32) = (((a ^ b) << 1) | ((a ^ b) >> 31)) ^ 0xffffffff
find g 1 snippets
# a database on 8-bit inputs is not consulted for 32-bit ones
snippets grow inputs 1 width 8 cost 2
find f 1 snippets
# 32 points do not tell every pair of 8-bit functions apart: a program
# that matches there and differs elsewhere is said, not listed
h(a: u8) = a == 77 ? 0 : a + 1
find h 1 snippets
# a file: started over, then grown on from where it stopped
snippets grow snipt fresh inputs 1 width 8 cost 1
snippets grow snipt inputs 1 width 8 cost 2
k(a: u8) = (a + a) * 2
find k 3 snippets snipt
# another shape than the file's is refused, naming both
snippets grow snipt inputs 2 width 8 cost 2
